## 11. Things You Must Never Do

- ❌ Never write a raw SQL query outside a `.model.js` file.
- ❌ Never call `fetch()`/`axios()` to an LLM provider outside `llm/llmClient.js`.
- ❌ Never duplicate load-balancing or injury logic outside `ruleEngine`.
- ❌ Never put a new model in a central `models/` folder — it belongs inside its module.
- ❌ Never let `ranking` or `social` modules write directly to `progress`'s tables — always go through `progress.service.js`.
- ❌ Never hardcode a config value (thresholds, API keys, tag lists) inside a service file.
- ❌ Never skip `responseFormatter.js` for API responses.

---

## 12. Git Commit Convention (Recommended)

```
<module>: short description

feat(plan): add injury-substitution check before saving plan
fix(session): correct latency issue in feedback loop
chore(config): update tier thresholds
```

This makes it trivial to trace which module a change touched, which
matters a lot once the team grows past 1-2 people.